{{> adminTop}}<div class="stats-grid"><div class="stat-card"><small>Students</small><strong>{{students}}</strong></div><div class="stat-card"><small>Courses</small><strong>{{courses}}</strong></div><div class="stat-card"><small>Learning attempts</small><strong>{{attempts}}</strong></div><div class="stat-card"><small>Credentials</small><strong>{{credentials}}</strong></div></div><div class="grid cols-2 space-top"><section class="card"><h2>Service health</h2><p class="chip">Database connection available</p><p>{{pending}} practical submissions awaiting grading.</p><p><a class="text-link" href="/healthz" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Check service health ↗</a></p><a class="button secondary" href="/admin/reports/export">Download learning report</a></section><section class="card"><h2>Backup & restore procedure</h2><ol class="workflow-list"><li>Use Aiven's database backup/export tooling and protect the export privately.</li><li>Before an upgrade, record the Git commit and take a database backup.</li><li>Restore to an isolated test database and verify account, course, file and credential counts.</li><li>Deploy the matching code version and run the additive migration.</li><li>Switch production only after testing the restored environment.</li></ol><p class="small muted">CSV reports are not full database backups. A database restore must be done by the hosting/database owner; this page does not run destructive restore commands.</p></section></div>{{> adminBottom}}
